# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-5 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-5 throughout: B5 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after B5's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# D5: the diagnosis repro again, WITH working triage. Run it only if an FX5 run fails or stalls (the fix is not accepted yet). The audits-off
# hang reproduction with the instruments on (c2-packed-tp4-diag: both verify audits off, the old tail, the stall watch at 120 s with its
# triage sidecar, the repaired trace census with no graph capture, the CCL handle guard in log mode); tp4-serve-5's image has ttexalens,
# so dump_running_operations and dump_callstacks must now read the hung mesh. If the stall fires, the log must hold '[TRIAGE-CHECK] ready'
# and '[TRIAGE dump_running_operations]' output naming the stuck op: that is the point of this job. '[TRIAGE-CHECK] UNAVAILABLE' means the image is wrong.
# Duration (estimate): 20-30 min; a stall costs the deadline plus triage, then the next job's reset.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-5
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-diag
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
